WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
Microplastics generate reactive oxygen species through surface interactions with water. This is Planetarian Daily, episode 251. A science deep dive, RNA at synapses, and two new tardigrade species from an Atlantic Sea Mount. Columbia University and University of California Berkeley researchers publish findings in nature, with science daily carrying the account, that as plastic particles break into smaller pieces, more surfaces exposed. Contact with water at those extra surfaces

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:35.200
then yields high energy radicals. Way men noted that such radicals are able to

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:41.660
harm animal and human tissue. In 2026 a federal program put $144 million

00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:47.454
toward research on toxic microplastics inside the body. Something most people get

00:00:47.454 --> 00:00:51.474
wrong is the belief that plastic sits chemically idle once it has broken into

00:00:51.474 --> 00:00:56.674
microscopic pieces. Hydrophobic surfaces change how water molecules and charge

00:00:56.674 --> 00:01:01.414
particles behave at the boundary. And that shift lets electrons move between species,

00:01:01.814 --> 00:01:06.354
so reactive oxygen species form right there rather than drifting in from somewhere else.

00:01:07.034 --> 00:01:12.034
After particles reach blood or tissues that hold abundant water, the same boundary chemistry

00:01:12.034 --> 00:01:18.794
can run inside a human body. Average concentrations reached roughly 240,000 plastic fragments per liter

00:01:18.794 --> 00:01:25.634
in bottled water. Most of them nanometer scale. A 2024 laser microscopy study that produced those

00:01:25.634 --> 00:01:29.634
counts already indicated far higher particle numbers than earlier estimates.

00:01:30.334 --> 00:01:35.094
Way Min's group traced the radicals directly to the plastic water interface, rather than

00:01:35.094 --> 00:01:36.874
to any additive or contaminant.

00:01:37.274 --> 00:01:41.734
That interface chemistry supplies one concrete mechanism that could connect documented

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:47.614
microplastic exposure to reported associations with cardiovascular and neurological conditions.

00:01:48.214 --> 00:01:52.794
What remains uncertain is the quantitative contribution of this pathway to actual tissue

00:01:52.794 --> 00:01:53.694
damage in people.

00:01:53.694 --> 00:01:58.914
One practical step is to reduce unnecessary plastic contact with food and water.

00:01:59.998 --> 00:02:05.438
Ribbonucleic acid or RNA acts as a scaffold that organizes the protein synapses in one

00:02:05.438 --> 00:02:10.598
into condensates at neurotransmitter release sites, according to work from Duke University

00:02:10.598 --> 00:02:15.878
and Charitay Berlin University Institute of Biochemistry, published in Advanced Science

00:02:15.878 --> 00:02:17.718
and described by Fizz.org.

00:02:18.118 --> 00:02:23.158
The work combined imaging in live neurons with a reconstituted system that showed translation

00:02:23.158 --> 00:02:29.398
happening in place. Amy Gladfelter and Dragameer Milovanovich led the team, which included

00:02:29.398 --> 00:02:35.438
Branislava Rankovich and Zachary Geisterfer. The results establish a structural job for R&amp;A

00:02:35.438 --> 00:02:41.166
beyond caring information. Sengor Seamount off Cape Verde produced two new armored

00:02:41.166 --> 00:02:46.186
tardigrade species after researchers from Sankenberg, Amir, examined Seamount sediment.

00:02:46.186 --> 00:02:55.646
They described megastigarctides hecate and peristigarctus poterta from 219 specimens and 212 of those

00:02:55.646 --> 00:03:01.786
animals came from the summit. The plateau supported 20 tardigrade taxa while a deep sea reference

00:03:01.786 --> 00:03:09.186
site 100 kilometers away supported only two. Megastigarctides hecate carries rare genital spines and

00:03:09.186 --> 00:03:15.986
turned up at about 100 meters depth. Peristigarctus poterta shows pedomorphism with a smaller

00:03:15.986 --> 00:03:17.266
body and fewer claws.

00:03:18.558 --> 00:03:22.678
Mitochondria keep a bacterial ancestry and assemble ribosomes of their own.

00:03:23.358 --> 00:03:28.378
A newly identified parasite protein clarifies a step in that assembly pathway, and how

00:03:28.378 --> 00:03:32.038
mitochondria build the machinery they need for their own protein synthesis.

00:03:33.265 --> 00:03:38.225
Bumblebees carry out sophisticated tasks, even though their brains are far smaller than conventional

00:03:38.225 --> 00:03:41.065
models treat as necessary for that kind of performance.

00:03:41.065 --> 00:03:41.845
conventions.

00:03:42.145 --> 00:03:47.065
Conventional assumptions tie larger brains to greater intelligence, and this result challenges

00:03:47.065 --> 00:03:51.105
a direct link between brain size and cognitive ability across species.

00:03:52.235 --> 00:03:57.815
Kvantified tested its beast VQE algorithm on dispersion interactions in a pair of molecules

00:03:57.815 --> 00:04:04.475
taken from a deoxyribonucleic acid, or DNA structure, running the calculation on Continuum

00:04:04.475 --> 00:04:06.795
System Model H2 quantum computer.

00:04:06.795 --> 00:04:10.775
The outputs match the established CCSDT method.

00:04:11.295 --> 00:04:17.535
The team cut the number of active orbitals from 236 to 53 and still held that accuracy.

00:04:18.215 --> 00:04:23.075
Hardware runs at two molecular geometries came out nearly identical to ideal simulations,

00:04:23.575 --> 00:04:28.175
showing a hybrid quantum classical route for studying molecular stacking that matters for

00:04:28.175 --> 00:04:28.995
drug discovery.

00:04:30.245 --> 00:04:36.125
DESY and European XFEL produced and transported flashes at 30,000 electron volts.

00:04:36.125 --> 00:04:42.425
The wavelength reached 0.04 nanometers, shorter than typical distances between neighboring

00:04:42.425 --> 00:04:43.445
atoms and solids.

00:04:44.045 --> 00:04:49.905
Reliable operation at that energy on the European XFEL facility improves spatial resolution

00:04:49.905 --> 00:04:51.125
for material studies.

00:04:51.991 --> 00:04:57.611
Barium Titanate had its refractive index and extinction coefficient map from 190 nanometers

00:04:57.611 --> 00:05:01.371
to 40 micrometers by KIST and Caltech researchers.

00:05:01.371 --> 00:05:07.171
In measurements carried by science daily, using Mueller-Matrix spectroscopic ellipsometry

00:05:07.171 --> 00:05:12.751
on single crystal samples, in the 2 to 10 micrometer range, extinction coefficients reached

00:05:12.751 --> 00:05:16.691
approximately 10 to the minus 5, a sign of very low absorption.

00:05:17.271 --> 00:05:21.551
The group also developed a method to predict behavior in crystals that contain multiple

00:05:21.551 --> 00:05:22.011
domains.

00:05:22.671 --> 00:05:27.451
The number-support design of optical modulators that rely on the material's pockles effect.

00:05:27.451 --> 00:05:34.639
Texas A&amp;M AgriLife research scientists in work described by Fizz.org developed a modified

00:05:34.639 --> 00:05:40.639
hampline with no measurable tetrahydrocanabinoid or THC and no additional cannabinoids.

00:05:41.119 --> 00:05:44.779
That trait could lower the risk of crop destruction under current regulations.

00:05:45.821 --> 00:05:50.401
Mushrooms served as a proxy for agricultural crops when Penn State researchers tested

00:05:50.401 --> 00:05:55.241
a lightweight model that watches drought, disease, or nutrient stress through non-destructive

00:05:55.241 --> 00:05:55.781
imaging.

00:05:55.781 --> 00:06:00.921
The approach keeps accuracy while using less computing power than some existing artificial

00:06:00.921 --> 00:06:02.861
intelligence, or AI methods.

00:06:03.945 --> 00:06:08.885
A new bioinformatics toolkit connects viruses to their bacterial and archaeal hosts at

00:06:08.885 --> 00:06:09.865
planetary scale.

00:06:10.485 --> 00:06:14.625
The resource tackles the problem of linking viruses that cannot be grown in laboratories

00:06:14.625 --> 00:06:20.165
to the hosts they actually infect, and it lets researchers study how viruses shape microbiome

00:06:20.165 --> 00:06:22.605
processes beyond simply killing those hosts.

00:06:22.605 --> 00:06:28.766
In brief, Indian researchers developed cancer spot, which medical dialogues reports detected

00:06:28.766 --> 00:06:36.166
72% of cancer cases with a 1.4% false positive rate in an independent validation group of participants

00:06:36.166 --> 00:06:40.506
across 14 cancer types using blood DNA methylation patterns.

00:06:41.086 --> 00:06:47.346
Blue sucker fish in Montana lived up to 130 years, in work carried by Fizz.org, with

00:06:47.346 --> 00:06:52.706
bomb radiocarbon dating of odoliths showing some individuals hatched in the late 1800s,

00:06:52.866 --> 00:06:55.486
more than tripling previous age estimates for the species.

00:06:56.106 --> 00:07:00.546
Before we go, further independent measurements of radical production rates inside living

00:07:00.546 --> 00:07:05.266
systems would clarify whether this plastic water chemistry scales to meaningful biological

00:07:05.266 --> 00:07:05.926
effects.

